<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91168" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πτερύ̆γ-ωμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the wings</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Horap.
				2.118
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>anything that spreads like a wing:—flap of the
			ear</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.701
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>part of the pudenda muliebria</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.16
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.114
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.174
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>part of a ballista</i>, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Vitr.
				10.11.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>group of letters</i> written so as to resemble a wing, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Leid.W.</u>
				20.26
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>V.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συκὴ ἐν πτέρναις</span>
			, in horses, v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Hippiatr.</u>
				82
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
